/-!
# Solvable-member preparation for 13.6.13

The minimal solvable choice, faithful binary action, and invariance and
nontriviality of the actual U_X are proved. The factor-construction target
retains the actual S₃ inclusions and double-commutator supports. Once its
construction and the orbit argument are supplied, the marked seed gives
U_X = U_H and [U_H,L_v] ≠ 1 through the checked consumer.

The normal S₃ product still has to be constructed from the complete B.5.6
alternatives. The transitivity, irreducibility and factor identification
still have to be proved. Thus this module does not yet assert 13.6.13.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, p.929.
-/
